Z||000014||mwbackus||01-28-2000||07:12 AM||||No, the hydraulic lifters in Fiero V6 are self-adjusting.<P><BR>Note:  Even boring chemists can kid around once in a while.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000015||WKDFIRO||01-28-2000||01:26 PM||||Ooooooohhhhh, Chemist humor.....<P>MrFiero describes only the rear valve cover removal. The easiest one to get too. Of course nothing ever happens to the exhaust manifold or the valve cover you can get to! If it is as easy as he says it is than have at! The rear valve covers, not only will you be splayed across your trunk and most of the engine you are going to be pretty much doing it by braille since you can't really see ANYTHING. If I was trying that, the last thing I would be capable of doing would be to muster the patience to manuever anything past the rocker arms!||||reg||1
Z||000016||DISenchanted||01-28-2000||07:09 PM||||Al, I'm sorry.  I don't know which one it is.  All I know is that I have oil comming out of the space between the valvecover and the block.  I'm more of an Electronics person so I'm not entirely sure.<P>I hope that Helps.  Atleast it's the easy one to get to.||||reg||1
Z||000017||mwbackus||01-28-2000||07:30 PM||||WKD, glad you enjoyed my sick sense of humor(eg..sarcasm).  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I too have never achieved removal of both valve covers with the intake plenum intact.  <P>DIS, I think we may be looking more towards the distributor O-ring. It is a very common source of oil leakage on the V6.  Its an easy repair, but it does require a subsequent reset of the timing.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000018||AL||01-28-2000||10:09 PM||||hey dis i would have to see it, we could get you fixed up in a hurry.||||reg||1
Z||000019||WKDFIRO||01-29-2000||03:49 AM||||Very true! Make sure it isn't something easy like the O-ring. Dealers charge outrageous prices when a simple $2 (dealer mark up for a 50 cent piece.)O ring is the culprit. Tricky thing that oil!<P>Mike I love sarcasm! But it get me into trouble sometimes.....:&gt;/||||reg||1
